course: dictionary
lesson: 13052
title: Words that hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fatso is a rude word. It is slang, and it is an insult: it is a nasty name for a fat person, used to make them feel bad. «The bully shouted, "Fatso!" across the playground.» The clues are the shout and the other children looking away. Nobody is being kind here.
explain: Words like this are about how people's bodies look, and calling names hurts. People come in many shapes and sizes, and no body is a joke. If you hear someone called this name, tell a teacher or a trusted adult.
explain: Some people say fatso as a joke between friends, but it can still upset the person it is aimed at. Before you say a word, ask: would this make someone feel small? If yes, choose a different word or say nothing at all.
fact: Fatso is an insulting name for a fat person.
fact: Fatso is rude slang, so it is not a polite word to use at school or at home.
fact: Some friends use fatso as a joke nickname, but it can still upset the person it is aimed at.
fact: The plural can be written as fatsos or fatsoes.
fact: Fatso has no kind phrases; it is used to insult, not to describe someone kindly.
exercise: «The bully shouted "Fatso!" at Sam in the playground.» What does fatso mean here? | *An insulting name for a fat person | A kind name for a friend | A type of sweet
exercise: Ella says, «Fatso is just a joke, so it's fine to say it to my best friend.» What is the best reply? | Yes, a joke is always fine | It is a kind and polite word | Say it more loudly so everyone laughs | *It can still upset your friend, so do not use it
exercise: Which word in this sentence is the rude slang? «The bully called Sam a fatso at lunch.» | lunch | bully | *fatso | called
test: What should you do if you hear someone shouting fatso at a classmate? | Say it more loudly | Join in to be funny | Laugh and say it too | *Tell a teacher or a trusted adult
test: Which sentence describes a friend kindly and does not insult anyone? | «Sam is a fatso, ha ha.» | *«Sam is a kind, funny friend.» | «Look at that fatso!»
exam: Which statement about fatso is correct? | It has no meaning at all | *It is rude and can hurt, even when said as a joke | It is a type of food | It is a polite word for a good friend
